{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1476231-how-can-vampires-get-away-with-so-much-when-auspex-exists","id":1476231,"title":"How can vampires get away with so much when auspex exists?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-11T15:28:07-08:00","id":1476231,"title":"How can vampires get away with so much when auspex exists?","content":"Even a 13th generation kindered can read minds, astral project, and even use spirits touch, as long as they specialize in auspex. How can anything stay hidden when some malkavian, tremere, or toreador can just astral project and enter their rivals haven and use telepathy to learn all their secrets.<br /> <br /> Plus its untraceable, no ones going to know that you read their mind.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised the clans with auspex haven't used dominate and presence to create an army of loyal followers from the safety of their haven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":27313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","user":"Hello","date":". 03-11-2022, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T16:12:12-08:00","id":1476235,"title":"","content":"[Revised/V20] Well, the real Game Breakers from that perspective are Auspex 4 and Auspex 5. Auspex 4 requires a Willpower to use on another Vamp, and Auspex 5 requires one regardless. That's a pretty big barrier to using them willy nilly. Still, being able to rip your rival's secrets from their trusted Ghoul's head is pretty sick. <br /> <br /> The real question is, why haven't a coterie of Tremere with Auspex 5 and any appreciable level of Lure of Flames captured a couple Sabbat shovelheads, used Blood Walk to track their lineage back to Caine, then gone Astral and roasted them all with Spontaneous Vampire Combustion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T16:25:56-08:00","id":1476236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1476231-how-can-vampires-get-away-with-so-much-when-auspex-exists?p=1476235#post1476235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Revised/V20] Well, the real Game Breakers from that perspective are Auspex 4 and Auspex 5. Auspex 4 requires a Willpower to use on another Vamp, and Auspex 5 requires one regardless. That's a pretty big barrier to using them willy nilly. Still, being able to rip your rival's secrets from their trusted Ghoul's head is pretty sick.<br /> <br /> The real question is, why haven't a coterie of Tremere with Auspex 5 and any appreciable level of Lure of Flames captured a couple Sabbat shovelheads, used Blood Walk to track their lineage back to Caine, then gone Astral and roasted them all with Spontaneous Vampire Combustion?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If they did that, then they would have to change the tone of the game from one of politics, to vampire wizards summoning storms and shooting fireball at each other. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T17:04:53-08:00","id":1476239,"title":"","content":"These aren't automatic powers, they have difficulties attached to them, and frequently require multiple successes.<br /> <br /> As well, characters need a reason to do something. Looking for information you don't know to look for in the first place isn't really functional. You keep secrets by... keeping them secret. If an Auspex user has no idea about something you did, why are they going to try to go looking for information about it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T17:12:36-08:00","id":1476240,"title":"","content":"There are certain limits when using Auspex that the ST needs to keep in mind.<br /> <br /> First, you often need to roll many successes in order to learn anything truly useful. Usually only having one or two successes won't tell you a whole lot.<br /> <br /> Second, the difficulty can be harder than expected. Spirit's Touch require that the items handled have real emotional connection to the person. The ST should make the DC high if it isn't. Or the difficulty is against the subject's Willpower. The ordinary schlubs of the world may not have much resistance, but anyone who has really valuable information likely has a high Willpower.<br /> <br /> Third, the high level powers often require Willpower expenditure. It's not something a resource you can regain easily. You need to limit your use. And using telepathy on other vampires and supernatural creatures always requires spending of Willpower.<br /> <br /> Fourth, the ST isn't supposed to come out and give the vampire direct information. Telepathy and Spirit's Touch reveals information in a series of visions that the vampire is suppose to put together and understand. For convenience or ease of the game, an ST can easily provide the final result directly to a PC (you realize that the visions mean...), but the ST is doing a favor to the player to expedite the game. What is really suppose to happen is that the vampire needs to interpret those random stream of consciousness pieces of information correctly. The ST has a lot of leeway in terms of what it is the telepathic vampire is picking up. There's no guarantee it'll ever be useful.<br /> <br /> Fifth, there's several things to remember about Astral Projection. It always requires Willpower, restricting its use. Furthermore, changes in destinations, prolonged scenes, etc. always require additional Willpower spends. A single night's attempt at projection can wipe out a lot of Willpower. The projector is not able to interact with the physical world as he is in some sort generic spirit plane. In other words, it can't actually be used to spy on people while the astral body is in the astral plane because you are not seeing the actual physical world. He needs to manifest as a ghostly form into the physical world first. And while the wording in all editions is not clear, I've always interpreted it that the astral projector can't attempt to use telepathy unless he is manifesting. The section on using telepathy or other Auspex is always found in the same paragraph after mentioning the need to manifest before interacting with the physical plane. And of course, once you manifest, the possibility of you being detected increases, especially if the person you are attempting to spy on also has Auspex or is somehow spiritually endowed. Lastly, the character is not alone in the &quot;astral plane&quot;. As written, it's some generic combination of all the actual umbras in the game which can give the ST a lot of room for interacting with it. All kinds of mages, lupines, wraiths, spirits, and other bizarre entities could be encountered. While in practice I think most STs simply ignore this point (I've never seen an ST actually bother to have interaction), it should be happening. And not all of these encounters might be neutral or benevolent. They might be annoying or hostile. There's all sorts of possible NPC interactions in the astral plane (although again, this is something I see STs ignoring because the power seems to be rarely used and there's little ST guidance given on this subject.)<br /> <br /> In short, a vampire can't astral project into a rival vampire's haven and simply learn all their secrets using telepathy. That vampire is going to spend multiple Willpower points to even attempt to do it, manifest nearby them, and hope they get enough successes to collect enough stream of consciousness thoughts (what if the vampire is just thinking about how a burger might taste just then?) that it leads to something possibly useful. But probably not - because it's just a random attempt at mind reading at a random point in the night without anything that would cause the vampire to think of actually important secret stuff right then.<br /> <br /> Obviously Auspex should provide real benefits to the characters who have it. But it's not meant to be something that provides all the answers or without drawbacks. It is exhausting on Willpower and usually provides only fleeting information which must be interpreted correctly. In terms of the setting, it's just another way to provide some additional clues. Very useful, but it doesn't provide omniscience. In terms of an ST providing information to PCs, the ST needs to make sure it isn't abused. If it is used sparingly, the ST should err on making it useful to the PC. If the PC seems to be abusing the power, the ST should actually run it as its written and make the player put in a lot more effort figuring things out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T20:57:53-08:00","id":1476254,"title":"","content":"I think <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=71HG4F0QXyc\" target=\"_blank\">this depiction of astral projection</a> is both wonderfully atmospheric and demonstrates some of the pitfalls of using the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-11T22:46:53-08:00","id":1476259,"title":"","content":"Doctor Sleep is probably a bit more Mage than VtM when it comes to astral projection pitfalls. Keeping to King adaptations, the memory warehouse in Dreamcatcher is also a good example of things, but a bit more one sided as Mr. Gray vs. Jonesy is a lot closer to how little you can &quot;counter-attack&quot; Auspex. But Dreamcatcher does touch on just how much stuff is rattling around in most people's heads,and how memories can be subjective and change overtime. How someone remembers something isn't always exactly how it happened. Jonesy knows he's fighting a losing battle against Mr. Gray, but it's a stall for time in hopes that Mr. Gray can't find the secrets he's looking for as there's a clock ticking in the plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T15:10:51-08:00","id":1476287,"title":"","content":"Auspex is broken from another perspective: learning<br /> The ability to read the mind of mortals allow the vampire to learn directly in their mind how work a car like they was watching a youtube video with all the experience of the target. <br /> <br /> More: by reading in the mind of a Vampire he could learn to use new Disciplines, a Tremere could learn the Vicissitude secrets by reading the mind of a Tzimisce prisoner before killing him to avoid blood bond.<br /> <br /> Of course it would require many success but not all vampires have 8 Willpower or more, and they could break the will of a prisoner through torture, poisons or drugs to reduce it's resistance","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T15:20:36-08:00","id":1476289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1476231-how-can-vampires-get-away-with-so-much-when-auspex-exists?p=1476287#post1476287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex is broken from another perspective: learning<br /> The ability to read the mind of mortals allow the vampire to learn directly in their mind how work a car like they was watching a youtube video with all the experience of the target.<br /> <br /> More: by reading in the mind of a Vampire he could learn to use new Disciplines, a Tremere could learn the Vicissitude secrets by reading the mind of a Tzimisce prisoner before killing him to avoid blood bond.<br /> <br /> Of course it would require many success but not all vampires have 8 Willpower or more, and they could break the will of a prisoner through torture, poisons or drugs to reduce it's resistance</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I always thought that this could be possible, and made me question why vampires didn't just capture one tremere and learn, all the secrets they knew on blood sorcery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T16:07:28-08:00","id":1476294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1476231-how-can-vampires-get-away-with-so-much-when-auspex-exists?p=1476287#post1476287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex is broken from another perspective: learning<br /> The ability to read the mind of mortals allow the vampire to learn directly in their mind how work a car like they was watching a youtube video with all the experience of the target.<br /> <br /> More: by reading in the mind of a Vampire he could learn to use new Disciplines, a Tremere could learn the Vicissitude secrets by reading the mind of a Tzimisce prisoner before killing him to avoid blood bond.<br /> <br /> Of course it would require many success but not all vampires have 8 Willpower or more, and they could break the will of a prisoner through torture, poisons or drugs to reduce it's resistance</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This kind of breaks the game completely.<br /> <br /> If you think about it, ALL knowledge skills are things that anyone with some kind of memory reading(be it Auspex, gifts or the mind sphere) can learn instantly.<br /> <br /> Heck, reading a few books or a youtube How-To tutorial can get someone the equivalent of 2 dots(I.E. a functional understanding) in any knowledges. That's literally how it works IRL. That's before you get into things like the years of public schooling, the impact of the internet on rapid learning, and other things of that nature.<br /> <br /> WOD is just kind of bad at simulating what people should realistically know because that's kind of necessary for the game to remain challenging. If the WOD splats actually had to content against IRL people rather than the dumbed-down versions they're used to, they'd get exposed and then promptly curb-stomped to extinction in a decade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T16:20:52-08:00","id":1476295,"title":"","content":"Using Auspex to learn seems a stretch at best, and inefficient even if you allow it. Each success gets you one piece of information. You'd have to net hundreds of successes to justify Drive 1 or 2. Even more so because you get the information in dream logic, not YouTube videos.<br /> <br /> Even if you can learn something about Disciplines, in at least V20 you have to drink blood from your teacher to learn the first dot. You can't just Auspex-steal Disciplines like that. There's also the addition WP cost, and the additional success cost as more secretive information requires more successes to get (and you're still getting one bit of information at a time).<br /> <br /> The Ability ratings are a bit screwed up, but mostly because they weren't that screwed up in '91, but things have changed in 31 years.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T18:23:21-08:00","id":1476301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1476231-how-can-vampires-get-away-with-so-much-when-auspex-exists#post1476231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even a 13th generation kindered can read minds, astral project, and even use spirits touch, as long as they specialize in auspex. How can anything stay hidden when some malkavian, tremere, or toreador can just astral project and enter their rivals haven and use telepathy to learn all their secrets.<br /> <br /> Plus its untraceable, no ones going to know that you read their mind.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised the clans with auspex haven't used dominate and presence to create an army of loyal followers from the safety of their haven.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are several factors why this doesn't really play out the way it should seem to.<br /> <br /> 1. Vampiric Population<br /> By canon there are not a lot of vampires in any given city at any given time, except for plot point extreme scenarios. If there are half a dozen vampires in a city and one scans another to find out their personal fetishes or embarrassing memories, it really won't matter to the other four vampires. <br /> <br /> 2. Inconsistent Focus<br /> The clans/bloodlines who have auspex as a default tend to have very different goals and structures. The Malks are crazy and disunited, the Toreadors tend to be more focused on their spheres of interest than greater goals, the Tzimisce are generally educated &amp; strategic but are bogged down by being tied to their homelands in concept as much as in mechanics, and finally the Tremere would be the only example of a clan that has a united power structure and strong leadership that could make use of Auspex recon except the writers can't seem to stop messing the clan. If anything Auspex is a good reason why the Tremere survived as long as they did.<br /> <br /> 3. People aren't Creative<br /> Despite the vast number of mechanics in V:tM that would allow a vampire to fight and destroy their foes at a distance, without the need for personal combat, most STs construct storylines that requires in person drama and many players have a desire for characters doing things they wouldn't dream of doing IRL, so they make combat characters. So doing things like using auspex recon to completely take apart an enemy organization really don't get used often. This gets very problematic when you have a mismatch between ST and Players, if one thinks this way and the other do not, the game will quickly implode.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-12T21:52:35-08:00","id":1476314,"title":"","content":"Most princes aren't secure enough that they can execute other vampires on the flimsy pretense of &quot;I read his mind, he's guilty&quot; especially as most other vampires are young and can't read minds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T03:38:04-07:00","id":1476320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1476231-how-can-vampires-get-away-with-so-much-when-auspex-exists?p=1476295#post1476295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each success gets you one piece of information. You'd have to net hundreds of successes to justify Drive 1 or 2. Even more so because you get the information in dream logic, not YouTube videos.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends of how big is the information. To learn how to drive, one sucess learn to use the car's pedals, another one to use the gearshift, a few more to learn traffics laws (the ST will fix the amount, let's say 30) and after getting all the success the PC spend his experience to buy the first dot of driving.<br /> The final word is to the ST and if he's ok how the PC will do it: using dominate to force a higher generation to teach you his secrets and using Auspex to speed up the learning is pretty easy on a Vampire with low Willpower (or drugged with poisoned blood to reduce his resistance). At the contrary if the PC try to steal his knowledge during a lambda conversation on a low generation Tremere with high willpower, the he has absolutly no chance of learning any important information.<br /> <br /> As always it all depends on the ST and the interpretation of the player, learning Thaumaturgy that way could be the objective of an entire scenario or at least many session of game to find a good target, approch him, take him down and only then trying to steal his knowledge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T13:01:22-07:00","id":1476334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1476231-how-can-vampires-get-away-with-so-much-when-auspex-exists?p=1476320#post1476320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends of how big is the information.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it doesn't. The book says one piece of information per success. More complicated or &quot;big&quot; information costs more successes. This is also important considering how Auspex treats the mind as &quot;layered&quot; and deeper layers cost more successes. Trying to learn to drive from someone not actively thinking about driving costs you even more successes.<br /> <br /> When, exactly, does this get easier than just using Dominate or Presence to get a mortal to teach you to drive the normal way, but at night?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To learn how to drive, one sucess learn to use the car's pedals, another one to use the gearshift, a few more to learn traffics laws (the ST will fix the amount, let's say 30) and after getting all the success the PC spend his experience to buy the first dot of driving. </div> </div> </div>Right. So netting 30 successes (which I think is low for how the book phrases things) just to learn Drive 1 (and still spending the normal XP on it!) using the 4th dot in a Discipline. Why bother?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> using dominate to force a higher generation to teach you his secrets and using Auspex to speed up the learning is pretty easy on a Vampire with low Willpower (or drugged with poisoned blood to reduce his resistance). </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that Auspex is irrelevant compared to the Dominate and blood-drugging going on in this scenario. If you're already using Dominate to compel a vampire to teach you a Discipline, what do you need Auspex for? Maybe Auspex 1 to make sure your commands are working and they're not trying to play along and trick you, but what does Telepathy add to any of this?<br /> <br /> If people are worried that Auspex is too strong, using &quot;ST interpretation,&quot; taken to wild extremes of what the Discipline is stated to be capable of seems strange to me. And no amount of Auspex is going to get past having to get one step blood bound to your &quot;teacher&quot; for a Discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-13T16:14:32-07:00","id":1476346,"title":"","content":"Then maybe it's a translation issue of my book (the v20 edition), at telepathy my book say that one success give one recent informations or allow to go further in the memory of the targer, it give the exemple of a 2 years old memory requiring 3 success (1 for reading and 2 per years), and deep secrets or forgotten memory require 5 success to read them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T09:39:25-07:00","id":1476384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1476231-how-can-vampires-get-away-with-so-much-when-auspex-exists?p=1476287#post1476287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auspex is broken from another perspective: learning<br /> The ability to read the mind of mortals allow the vampire to learn directly in their mind how work a car like they was watching a youtube video with all the experience of the target.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think someone can learn to drive a car from watching a YouTube video then you're going to be spending a lot of money on repairs. While it might give someone the process of how to start a car and what the controls do it takes a lot of learning to be able to drive safely in real conditions.<br /> <br /> This kind of 'magical thinking' is a serious problem in modern games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T11:14:51-07:00","id":1476389,"title":"","content":"That's why i also said that it would require many success (dozens) just to be able to buy the first dot in driving","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T13:08:33-07:00","id":1476394,"title":"","content":"The problem is that most Abilities, even Knowledges, have enough practical things you need to actually do and experience doing to justify buying dots in them that just reading minds isn't really enough to learn them.<br /> <br /> No matter how aware you are of things like idling speeds and how different cars (even of the same model) can have variations in how much pressure it takes to engage pedals, there's a gap between theoretical knowledge and practical knowledge. There's a reason why any decent driver's ed class includes actually driving cars at some point: you need to experience it for yourself.<br /> <br /> There's a difference between being in law-school, and arguing a case in a real court. There's a difference between studying anatomy and doing actual surgery. Etc. There's just a cap in how human brains are wired before &quot;book&quot; learning stops being useful compared to actually doing the tasks in question.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T19:20:59-07:00","id":1476411,"title":"","content":"Also isn't there a part regarding telepathy being a vague mixture of images, sensations, and emotions, rather than it being a tutorial video?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-14T19:30:38-07:00","id":1476412,"title":"","content":"Yep. We've tried to point out that aspect as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T12:54:37-07:00","id":1476451,"title":"","content":"Bearing in mind the comparison to YouTube made before there's an interesting parallel with that modern trend of people thinking they are experts after watching a few videos on the internet!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T17:10:49-07:00","id":1476475,"title":"","content":"Never talked about becoming expert, just the possibility of learning through the mind of a target and after that practice by yourself to be able to buy the first dot of an ability. <br /> The first dot being equal to a novice level of what you can do, we're far from an &quot;expert&quot; level","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T19:18:36-07:00","id":1476486,"title":"","content":"But it never actually addresses the fundamental issue:<br /> <br /> What's the benefit of Auspex mining a human's brain to learn a lot about driving a car? You're still going to have to go out and learn to drive for yourself anyway. Nobody is making a case that &quot;learning&quot; with Auspex is a problem because it's clear that you can't use Auspex to really short cut anything (in the already highly abstract learning system of the game).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T20:49:15-07:00","id":1476495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1476231-how-can-vampires-get-away-with-so-much-when-auspex-exists?p=1476486#post1476486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But it never actually addresses the fundamental issue:<br /> <br /> What's the benefit of Auspex mining a human's brain to learn a lot about driving a car? You're still going to have to go out and learn to drive for yourself anyway. Nobody is making a case that &quot;learning&quot; with Auspex is a problem because it's clear that you can't use Auspex to really short cut anything (in the already highly abstract learning system of the game).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's why drive isn't a knowledge skill.<br /> <br /> This type of abuse would only work for knowledges, if the ST allowed it for some reason","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-15T22:13:47-07:00","id":1476498,"title":"","content":"As I've point out though, it doesn't even work for Knowledges, because they're not just &quot;roll to know a thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> You can't learn how to effectively do good library research from Academics by spamming Auspex. You can't learn how to do proper first aid, or know how to do a calculus proof, or write a proper legal memo, or perform an occult ritual, etc. etc. etc. via Auspex. Knowledges are still Abilities that involve learning how to do things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T03:06:43-07:00","id":1476513,"title":"","content":"I agree that Auspex does not work like in matrix, you're not &quot;dowloading&quot; the knowledge of your target, you only see them (by flash, not as a video, you were right). That mean you still need practice to actually learn something. But where i don't understand the reasoning is why with a lot of success it would not count as at least a short lesson?<br /> <br /> I mean in real life if you're talking with a scientist and he is trying to explain how work the human body, the nervous system for example, he will use a lot of technical terms you don't know and you wont understand everything, but if you can read in his mind and instantly get at least a clue on the meaning of the words he is using and combine what he's saying with the informations you read in his mind you will be able to understand way more easily his lessons. The book seems clear to me: 1 success = 1 information, more if it's an old memory and at least 5 for a deep secret or forgotten memory.<br /> To get back on the driving, of course you won't be able to drive after 5 minutes reading the mind of someone but with time AND practice you will learn how to drive at least as a novice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T04:09:50-07:00","id":1476515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1476231-how-can-vampires-get-away-with-so-much-when-auspex-exists?p=1476513#post1476513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IBut where i don't understand the reasoning is why with a lot of success it would not count as at least a short lesson?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that it wouldn't &quot;count&quot; it's just such an epic waste of time to do so. All of the time this Auspex user is spending parsing the dream-thoughts of some random human to learn about driving could have been far more productively spent: reading, using lower level Disciplines to get the human to explain things directly, pay a teacher, etc.<br /> <br /> Why would a vampire bother?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean in real life if you're talking with a scientist and he is trying to explain how work the human body, the nervous system for example, he will use a lot of technical terms you don't know and you wont understand everything, but if you can read in his mind and instantly get at least a clue on the meaning of the words he is using and combine what he's saying with the informations you read in his mind you will be able to understand way more easily his lessons. </div> </div> </div>1) Most scientists know how to modulate their words to their audience.<br /> <br /> 2) Information isn't understanding. Otherwise the scientist could just give you a pamphlet of definitions and so on and you'd be able to perfectly understand the lesson. <br /> <br /> For most science concepts there's the five minute super simple explanation for people that don't really need to understand how any of this works on any deep level and just need the bare-bones basics, the two-hour version for people that need some in-depth understanding but only on a very theoretical level, the month long version for people that need a solid practical grasp so they can apply it to some other pursuit, the years long version for people that deal with it on a professional basis, and the lifetime of study of people trying to answer these questions because we still don't actually know everything yet.<br /> <br /> Even if you're trying to get through easiest versions of a science lesson, there's still hundreds of them to justify Science 1 (or Medicine 1).<br /> <br /> On top of all of this, trying to read the mind of a scientist that isn't a skilled educator is most likely vastly less effective than just hiring a professional science educator instead. Teaching is its own set of skills... one that lots of people have. Instead of trying to use Auspex to piece together dream-logic information from someone' head.. why not just ask a teacher to teach you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To get back on the driving, of course you won't be able to drive after 5 minutes reading the mind of someone but with time AND practice you will learn how to drive at least as a novice </div> </div> </div>But what's the point if time and practice were going to be part of learning anyway?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T07:19:24-07:00","id":1476519,"title":"","content":"If it cannot be that efficient to learning new thing, isn't that effective to read the past of a target, need huge time to obtain what we need that could be obtain easier by other ways.... then why is it a level 4 power?<br /> <br /> The more you spent to mastering your disciplines the more powerfull you become, in other disciplines level 4 power are way more effective in their action.<br /> Considering how expensive is the cost of higher level of discipline it does not seems to worth it as you guys describe it \ud83e\udd14 or may be i'm missing something","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T08:32:03-07:00","id":1476521,"title":"","content":"It's useful for a lot of information gathering, it's just that it's not useful to learn Skills and Disciplines because that requires a lot of information, minutiae detail, practice and experience<br /> <br /> It's useful to do stuff like discovering a quick and dirty secret in a subtle fashion. For instance: If you suspect another vampire it's plotting against you (Like: leading you to a trap or ambush), you can use this to know about that in a way that's subtler than Dominate or Pressence (and much subtler than sequestering and drugging your target)<br /> <br /> In a society full of plots where you don't know who's your enemy, who's your enemy's enemy, who you can manipulate and how. A society where discretion and respecting the social graces it's a must if you don't want to be in everyone's hit list ... a subtle way to gather even fragments of information it's definitely a good tool to have. It's not perfect because it would break the setting, but it shouldn't be so vague that you can't gather valuable intel <br /> <br /> Also, ain't capped by your Generation, ain't automaticaly negated by Willpower, and is faster than bonding and/or torturing someone.<br /> <br /> But if you have the time and the cappability to capture and drug a Tremere, and then painstakingly pierce together all the details and information needed to learn even the 1rst level of Thaumaturgy (and practice what you see), when you don't even know what to look for or what the dangers of mispracticing Thaumaturgy with incomplete knowledge could be ... all of which I *would* allow, but it would take longer than regular teaching ... then you can probably use other methods (like, Bond the Tremere. Doesn't require a roll and you have a teacher that *likes* you so he will try to teach well and keep you safe)<br /> <br /> A power to gether intel doesn't need to be better than other ways *all* the time in order to be good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-16-2022, 11:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T09:05:57-07:00","id":1476523,"title":"","content":"Ok so that's possible but that's the complexity of the informations that make learning more dangerous and time consuming. <br /> That's clearer i thought that you were saying that's impossible to learn through the mind of another one, this is just longer and you cannot gather every details<br /> In clear you can use it to complete a puzzle in a case (like resolve a murder) but if you use it to learn something completely knew it's like putting together one by one each piece of an unknown puzzle that counts 1000 pieces","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T10:57:53-07:00","id":1476525,"title":"","content":"Auspex 4 is incredibly useful even if it isn't useful for justifying spending XP for more dots on your sheet.<br /> <br /> A lot of us are &quot;downplaying&quot; Auspex because the thread was &quot;overplaying&quot; it: people were treating Auspex as some &quot;instant win&quot; button when it comes to gathering information, so we're putting out all the flaws it has that make it not overpowered in that sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-16T12:48:30-07:00","id":1476528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1476231-how-can-vampires-get-away-with-so-much-when-auspex-exists?p=1476525#post1476525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of us are &quot;downplaying&quot; Auspex because the thread was &quot;overplaying&quot; it: people were treating Auspex as some &quot;instant win&quot; button when it comes to gathering information, so we're putting out all the flaws it has that make it not overpowered in that sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's difficult to see the limit of that kind of power \ud83d\ude05, especially when the target cannot feel that someone is reading his mind and even if he guesses he cannot resist it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 03-16-2022, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-19T03:56:35-07:00","id":1476719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1476231-how-can-vampires-get-away-with-so-much-when-auspex-exists?p=1476528#post1476528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's difficult to see the limit of that kind of power</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's worth looking at things from a higher perspective.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing that a majority of the people posting on this forum are long time players and StoryTellers. As such we've experienced the problems with allowing players to get away with the idea that they can 'do anything' with certain powers as this inevitably causes serious repercussions, and thus we tend to react by putting limits on those powers. <br /> <br /> An good example of this is the Spirit sphere in Mage. There's a phrase that goes around saying that all the effects can be duplicated by the Spirit sphere because with sufficient Spirit you can always call up a spirit who can do what you want to do. Now while this idea has some merit to it, it completely disregards the difficulty of actually doing this in practice, allowing players to handwave the difficulties and get away with anything, and the more crafty the player is and the less wise the ST is the worse it gets. This is such a common theme in RPGs that it even has it's own moniker: Power Playing<br /> <br /> So when someone comes along and asks, in all innocence, how to 'power play' the Auspex discipline (although not in those exact words) there's naturally going to be a negative reaction that downplays the discipline.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}